<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gilaks</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gilites</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gilaks are an Iranian people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilan">Gilan</a>, the humid lowland on the south-western shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>, who speak the Gilaki language. In early Islamic times the Gil and their Daylamite neighbours long resisted Arab rule, and in the late 9th and early 10th centuries many converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaydism">Zaydi Shia Islam</a> under the Alavid rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gilaks.jpg" alt="Gilaks" width="320" height="295" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Langroodi.gilak · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Gilak-inhabited_provinces_of_Iran,_according_to_a_poll_in_2011.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
